## Block D — AI processing flow and UI

## T12 — Processing and Apply flow on the server
Reasoning: Joins admission, dispatch, draft, authorization rechecks, and atomic Apply — the heart of FR-015–FR-021 — 
and owns every dispatch-dependent check (review P2–P5). Apply appends items as T2 (TRACK) established: call 
`private.meeting_note_lock_for_change(note_id, <NOT_FOUND token>)` (actor KEY SHARE → note FOR UPDATE; returns 
can_edit, note_revision), insert with creator snapshots and `assignee_name` whenever `assignee_id` is set; the item 
insert trigger raises 22023 MEETING_NOTE_ITEM_LIMIT_REACHED past 100 and the whole Apply rolls back; READ COMMITTED.
Task: A start route that, in order: verifies the ticket signature and the 24 h expiry of the ticket and its embedded 
key before any lookup (expired → rejected, no dispatch, even without records; a client-supplied key differing from the 
ticket's is rejected); compares the ticket's user/company/note with the authenticated application user; calls T9's 
admission RPC, which re-authorizes current membership and editor rights before anything else (existing operation → 
returns its pending/final/"discarded" status without dispatch, even if settings changed since; new operation → current 
membership, editor rights, and current settings revision required, stale revision → refused with the new provider 
name); runs T11's size preflight and, when it refuses or the client cancels before sending, settles the operation as 
never dispatched (released); otherwise dispatches once via T11 with the admitted snapshot, key, and transcript; 
resolves suggested names locally (exact full name, else unique first name, case/accent-insensitive, current members 
only); rechecks membership and note existence before returning; honors client abort (operation "discarded") with 
best-effort outbound abort; and settles usage. An `authenticated`-granted Apply RPC accepts the edited summary and 
accepted items only at the draft's source revision, rechecks rights in the transaction, marks suggestions duplicating 
existing items, appends accepted items under T2's shared per-note lock and capacity, writes the summary, and creates 
one version — or changes nothing.
Done when: Processing and Apply satisfy FR-015–FR-021 against the fake provider, including every dispatch-dependent 
usage, replay, and authorization outcome.
Verify by: Integration tests through the routes against local Supabase and the T16 server for AC-010 (draft changes 
nothing until Apply; Apply stores exactly edited summary and accepted items, one version), AC-012 (text received by 
the fake provider for .vtt/.srt has no cue numbers/timestamps/settings and keeps speakers), AC-013 (name matching; 
request contains no roster), AC-016 (each failure outcome's counting), AC-025 (stale notice refused; admitted 
operation completes on P), AC-026 (oversize refused, zero received requests, usage unchanged; cancellation before send 
releases the reservation), AC-027, AC-028 (concurrent starts dispatch once; replay received once), AC-029 (connection 
drop counted once; listed rejections not counted; unlisted/mid-stream counted), AC-030 (paused provider with 
transcript replacement / member removal), AC-032 (98 items: add vs two-item Apply; a settings save, an admission, and 
an Apply by that admin running concurrently on the same note all finish without a deadlock error), AC-034 
(cancelled-then-completed replay → "discarded"; expired ticket after record cleanup and with records retained; a fresh 
ticket cannot reuse an earlier key; replay after a settings change returns the original operation; a child process 
