1: -- Phase 6 T1 (spec-interview/phase-6-meeting-notes; FR-028, FR-029, FR-030,
2: -- BR-001, BR-007; AC-020, AC-021, AC-023, AC-031): meeting-note schema, read
3: -- isolation, and lifecycle contract.
4: --
5: -- Before this migration (baseline 20260610183000 / 20260610183139):
6: --   * public.meeting_notes had no company, author, revision, content,
7: --     participants, or versions; room_id was NOT NULL -> spaces ON DELETE
8: --     CASCADE (deleting a space deleted its notes); summary was NOT NULL.
9: --   * Both meeting-note SELECT policies joined through public.spaces, so a
10: --     note without a space would become invisible to everyone.
11: --
12: -- After this migration:
13: --   * public.meeting_notes carries
14: --       - company_id (NOT NULL -> companies ON DELETE CASCADE): deleting a
15: --         company deletes its notes; immutable for every role;
16: --       - author_user_id + author_name: historical snapshots of the creating
17: --         user's application users.id and display name; immutable, no FK, so
18: --         they survive the user row;
19: --       - created_by: the live reference to the author (-> users ON DELETE SET
20: --         NULL); at INSERT it must equal author_user_id; afterwards it can
21: --         only become NULL, and only once that user row no longer exists (the
22: --         FK action of a user deletion), never by a client or process;
23: --       - revision (bigint >= 1, never decreases), content (text, <= 100,000 chars, '' by
24: --         default), transcript_id (identity of the stored transcript; present
25: --         exactly when a transcript is stored);
26: --       - room_id nullable -> spaces ON DELETE SET NULL: deleting a space keeps
27: --         its notes (FR-028); a non-NULL room_id must be a space of the note's
28: --         company;
29: --       - summary optional (NULL = no summary; the non-empty check stays).
30: --   * public.meeting_note_participants (note_id, user_id, display_name,
31: --     sort_order 0..49): participants by application users.id (no FK, so a
32: --     deleted user keeps their place) with a display-name snapshot; at most 50
33: --     per note by construction (unique sort_order 0..49); identity and snapshot
34: --     immutable, sort_order mutable.
35: --   * public.meeting_note_versions: immutable snapshots (revision, title,
36: --     meeting_date, participants as a JSON array of {user_id, display_name}
37: --     with <= 50 entries, content, summary, editor_user_id + editor_name
38: --     snapshots, created_at). The live editor reference edited_by (-> users ON
39: --     DELETE SET NULL) is the only column that may change, and only to NULL
40: --     after that user row is gone. A version can be deleted only by the
41: --     cascade of its note's deletion (the note row is already gone).
42: --   * RLS: every read of notes, participants, versions, and action items is
43: --     scoped to the note's own company_id through
44: --     private.is_company_member(company_id) (users.supabase_uid =
45: --     auth.uid()::text and users.company_id = note.company_id); never through
46: --     public.spaces. A user removed from the company (users.company_id
47: --     cleared) loses read; the same users.id rejoining regains it.
48: --   * Grants: anon holds nothing and authenticated holds SELECT only on the
49: --     four tables; there is no client write path (write RPCs come in T17/T2).
50: --     service_role keeps SELECT/INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE (no TRUNCATE, REFERENCES,
51: --     TRIGGER on notes, participants, versions), and the guards below apply to
52: --     every role, including service_role and postgres; a statement guard
53: --     rejects TRUNCATE of notes, participants, and versions for every role
54: --     (row triggers do not fire on TRUNCATE).
55: --   * Trigger functions are owned by postgres, SECURITY DEFINER with
56: --     search_path '', and EXECUTE is revoked from PUBLIC, anon, authenticated,
57: --     and service_role (trigger functions need no EXECUTE grant to fire).
