3: -- search over meeting notes.
4: --
5: -- Before this migration (T1 20261013103447, T17 20261013105021, T2
6: -- 20261013110632): no search infrastructure; the unaccent extension is
7: -- available but not installed.
8: --
9: -- After this migration:
10: --   * Extension unaccent installed in schema `extensions` (Supabase
11: --     convention). ONLINE DEPENDENCY: the target must allow
12: --     `create extension unaccent with schema extensions`; if unaccent already
13: --     exists there in another schema, the dictionary reference
14: --     extensions.unaccent below fails and this file must be adapted (T8/T15
15: --     preflight checks it).
16: --   * Two text-search configurations:
17: --       private.meeting_notes_pt = portuguese, with word/hword/hword_part
18: --         mapped to (extensions.unaccent, portuguese_stem);
19: --       private.meeting_notes_en = english, with the same tokens mapped to
20: --         (extensions.unaccent, english_stem).
21: --     Why both: notes mix Portuguese and English. Every document is indexed
22: --     with BOTH configurations (vector = pt || en) and every query is parsed
23: --     with BOTH and OR-ed (pt-query || en-query), so a word matches when it
24: --     matches under either language's stemming ("meetings" ~ "meeting" via
25: --     english, "orçamentos" ~ "orçamento" via portuguese). Accents: unaccent
26: --     runs before the stemmer for non-ASCII tokens ("reunião" ~ "reuniao");
27: --     ASCII tokens carry no accents. Case: both stemmers lowercase ("Budget" ~
28: --     "budget"). A word is a stop word only if it is one in both languages.
29: --     A custom unaccented 'simple' config was rejected: it does no stemming,
30: --     so plural/singular and verb forms would not match.
31: --   * public.meeting_notes.search_vector: tsvector GENERATED ALWAYS AS
32: --     (private.meeting_note_search_document(title, content, summary)) STORED,
33: --     GIN-indexed. Weights: title A, summary B, content C. Content is indexed
34: --     as TEXT: private.meeting_note_plain_text removes every tag of the
35: --     sanitized HTML (tag names and attributes, e.g. href, are never indexed),
36: --     joins inline formatting (strong/b/em/i/a/span/label) without a space and
37: --     block boundaries with one, and decodes the entities the sanitizer emits
38: --     (&amp; &lt; &gt; &quot; &#39; &nbsp;). The transcript is NOT indexed.
39: --     Being a generated column, it is recomputed by Postgres on every insert
40: --     and on every update of title/content/summary, by any writer, in the same
41: --     row write: no trigger, no extra lock, no revision bump, no version (the
42: --     T1 guard and T17 versioning are untouched; the guard never sees a
43: --     search-only update because none exists).
44: --   * Action items: GIN expression index on
45: --     private.meeting_note_item_search_document(description) (unweighted =
46: --     weight D). Item writes never touch public.meeting_notes (T2): the index
47: --     entry is maintained by the item row's own insert/update/delete, so there
48: --     is no item -> note write, no lock taken on the note, and no interaction
49: --     with the capacity trigger's note FOR UPDATE lock. The items table shape
50: --     is unchanged (the item RPCs return to_jsonb(row)).
51: --   * public.search_meeting_notes(p_query text, p_room_id uuid,
52: --       p_space_removed boolean, p_meeting_from timestamptz,
53: --       p_meeting_to timestamptz, p_limit integer, p_offset integer)
54: --       RETURNS TABLE (note_id, room_id, title, meeting_date, author_user_id,
55: --         author_name, has_summary, has_transcript, revision, created_at,
56: --         updated_at, relevance real, excerpt_field text, excerpt text,
57: --         total_count bigint)
