59: --     authenticated only), applying the same rule as the RLS read policies
60: --     (BR-001, private.is_company_member): the caller is resolved by
61: --     users.supabase_uid = auth.uid()::text, and every note and item read in
62: --     the function is restricted to n.company_id = that users.company_id. A
63: --     caller without a users row or company gets no rows; members and admins
64: --     of another company never see a note (SM-3). Why not SECURITY INVOKER:
65: --     under RLS, Postgres evaluates the policy quals before any
66: --     non-leakproof user qual, and the full-text operator @@ is not
67: --     leakproof, so neither GIN index could ever be used (verified with
68: --     EXPLAIN: seq scans plus a per-item policy subplan, even with
69: --     enable_seqscan off); search cost would grow with every note and item of
70: --     the company.
71: --       - p_query blank/NULL: list mode — every note of the company within
72: --         the filters, meeting_date desc, id desc; relevance/excerpt NULL.
73: --       - otherwise websearch syntax (words AND-ed, "phrases", or, -word);
74: --         a query with no lexemes (only stop words / punctuation) returns no
75: --         rows. Matching: note vector OR any single one of its items; the
76: --         whole query (all words, any -word exclusion) is evaluated within one
77: --         document (the note's text, or one item), so words split between the
78: --         note text and an item do not combine. Relevance =
79: --         ts_rank(note vector, q, normalization 1) + max item ts_rank.
80: --         Order: relevance desc, meeting_date desc, note id desc (total order,
81: --         so offset pages have no duplicates or gaps while data is unchanged).
