spec-interview/phase-6-meeting-notes/reviews\PLAN-v3-reviewed.md:122:Task: Server-only usage records per company per 
day (America/Sao_Paulo). One `service_role`-only admission RPC that, in a single transaction holding the company 
settings row lock: (1) verifies the caller's current membership and editor rights on the note (for replays too); (2) 
looks up an existing operation for the ticket's idempotency key — if found with the same binding, returns its status 
without new admission, regardless of later settings or source changes; if found with a different binding, rejects; (3) 
otherwise, with the note row locked, verifies that the bound settings revision is current and that the note's revision 
and transcript identity equal the ticket's (stale source → conflict, nothing reserved), reserves usage against the 
limit, records the operation with the provider/model/effort snapshot, and returns the matching key and the bound 
transcript text from the same snapshot. Settlement once, against the admission day, by a `service_role`-only RPC; it 
counts every dispatched operation, refunds only pre-processing rejections, and releases the reservation (not counted) 
for an operation that demonstrably never sent a request (size preflight refusal, cancellation before send, error 
before dispatch); settlement is idempotent. The idempotency key is generated by the server at ticket issuance and 
embedded in the signed ticket (a client cannot choose a key or reuse one with a new ticket); the key expires with its 
ticket, 24 h after issuance, checked before any lookup or admission. Idempotency keys scoped to user+company+operation 
and bound to note id, source revision, transcript identity, settings revision. Signed processing tickets (issue time, 
idempotency key, user, company, note, source revision, transcript identity, settings revision) with HMAC-SHA256 using 
the required server-only env var `MEETING_NOTES_TICKET_SECRET` (≥32 bytes, no fallback — AI start refuses with a 
configuration error when missing), plus optional `MEETING_NOTES_TICKET_SECRET_PREVIOUS` accepted for verification only 
so a rotation keeps outstanding tickets valid for their 24 h; the local value is provisioned in `.env.local` and 
`.env.example` documents it. A ticket-issue route (called when the notice is shown) authorizes current membership and 
editor rights before signing. Operation records without content kept 30 days (pg_cron cleanup); an operation without 
outcome 10 minutes after dispatch becomes "failed" and stays counted (pg_cron); deleting notes or users never changes 
usage; no client role can read-modify usage beyond reading its own company's count.
spec-interview/phase-6-meeting-notes/reviews\PLAN-v3-reviewed.md:149:Task: Server-only adapters: Anthropic via 
`@anthropic-ai/sdk`, OpenAI via `openai`, Kimi and GLM via the OpenAI SDK with their OpenAI-compatible base URLs; SDK 
retries disabled (`maxRetries: 0`); each sends only the matrix's valid parameters for the chosen model and reasoning 
level; output requested and validated against one draft schema (summary sections, ≤100 items with description and 
assignee name as written); malformed/truncated output is a failure; an input-size preflight against the model's 
context/output budget refuses oversize transcripts before any request; provider errors are mapped to sanitized 
messages (no key, no transcript) and classified as pre-processing rejection only per the matrix. A server-only 
base-URL override selects the fake server; it is ignored and logged as refused when `NODE_ENV=production`, and no 
client input can set it.
spec-interview/phase-6-meeting-notes/reviews\PLAN-v3-reviewed.md:160:Task: A start route that, in order: verifies the 
ticket signature and the 24 h expiry of the ticket and its embedded key before any lookup (expired → rejected, no 
dispatch, even without records; a client-supplied key differing from the ticket's is rejected); compares the ticket's 
user/company/note with the authenticated application user; calls T9's admission RPC, which re-authorizes current 
membership and editor rights before anything else (existing operation → returns its pending/final/"discarded" status 
without dispatch, even if settings changed since; new operation → current membership, editor rights, and current 
settings revision required, stale revision → refused with the new provider name); runs T11's size preflight and, when 
it refuses or the client cancels before sending, settles the operation as never dispatched (released); otherwise 
dispatches once via T11 with the admitted snapshot, key, and transcript; resolves suggested names locally (exact full 
name, else unique first name, case/accent-insensitive, current members only); rechecks membership and note existence 
before returning; honors client abort (operation "discarded") with best-effort outbound abort; and settles usage. An 
`authenticated`-granted Apply RPC accepts the edited summary and accepted items only at the draft's source revision, 
rechecks rights in the transaction, marks suggestions duplicating existing items, appends accepted items under T2's 
shared per-note lock and capacity, writes the summary, and creates one version — or changes nothing.
