**Analyzing caching and API idempotency issues**

I’m looking into how cache-control headers interact with Next.js dynamic routes and browser caching, noting that 
`force-dynamic` doesn’t always guarantee no caching. I’m also thinking about how non-idempotent note-creation APIs 
might lead to duplicate notes on network failures and retries, which could cause UI and backend inconsistencies.
**Reviewing versioning and history limits**

I’m exploring how versioning handles exact-once semantics without enforcing idempotency, accepting that duplicates can 
happen in manual workflows without impacting performance. I’m also noting that the PostgREST API limits version 
listing to 1000 entries without pagination, which means full history restoration isn’t feasible through this endpoint.
